verses.tf_en:
① **«The Six Exemplary Destroyed Nations»** — Have these present-day hypocrites and deniers not received the harrowing historical chronicles of those before them?
1. The people of Nuh (drowned in the universal deluge);
2. The mighty 'Ad of Hud (shattered by a furious, howling gale);
3. The proud Thamud of Salih (seized by the catastrophic shriek and seismic convulsion);
4. The tyrannical people of Ibrahim (Nimrod and his cohorts decimated by humiliation);
5. The inhabitants of Madyan of Shu'ayb (incinerated beneath the fiery shadow of the day of the canopy);
6. The overturned cities (*al-Mu'tafikat*) of Lut (upended and pelted with marked stones of baked clay).
② **«اَتَتْهُمْ رُسُلُهُمْ بِالْبَیِّنٰتِ فَمَا كَانَ اللّٰهُ لِیَظْلِمَهُمْ وَلٰكِنْ كَانُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ یَظْلِمُوْنَ»** (Their Noble Messengers had brought clear proofs to them; so it did not befit Allah’s Majesty to oppress them, but in fact they wronged themselves) — Every messenger arrived equipped with undeniable miracles and lucid guidance, yet the nations chose obstinate arrogance and hostility. Allah never oppressed them; rather, through their own unyielding disbelief and persecution of the prophets, they brought ruin upon their own souls.
